= Adaptation in systems — Simple =

'''Adaptation''' is when a system changes because conditions change.

The change helps the system keep working, survive, or fit its environment better.

Adaptation can happen through learning, feedback, changing behavior, changing structure, or evolution.

It is not exactly the same as robustness.

Robustness means continuing to work despite disturbance; adaptation means changing in response to it.

